            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Athena33"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As a greek american living in Greece just a few suggestions. Make sure you drain as much juice from the cucumber before mixing. Use then about a 1/2 cup of extra virgin olive oil in the mixture to smooth it out. In Greece no one uses mustard so that is up to taste of anyone. It is best if it sits about 8 hours in fridge and put a piece of loaf bread on top so it will soak up extra moisture from cucumber. Remove bread before serving.",
            "datePublished": "2009-04-27T00:31:50.473Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "family of seven"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I also use yogurt instead of sour cream (who needs the calories!)\nAfter peeling the cuke, I cut it it chunks &amp; put it in my food chopper/processer. I, then put it in a metal strainer and squeeze the juice out. This works for me and my family loves it. I hope this is helpful.",
            "datePublished": "2011-02-10T08:22:11.717Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ben Huff"
            },
            "reviewBody": "ive been makin this for years now, it is an excellent base recipe as is but i feel ive perfected it. first, mix 50/50 greek yogurt and sour cream. cut out cucumber seeds and finely grate. omit mustard, not necessary, add a lil quality olive oil and a pinch of s+p and viola, perfection. also, fresh dill does make a difference",
            "datePublished": "2020-08-31T22:33:00.737Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BLUEROADS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Exactly what I wanted, thanks for a great recipe. I used 2 cucumbers and after shredding them put them in a dish towel and twisted it to remove as much \"water\" as possible. That is my only hint, the rest was wonderful!",
            "datePublished": "2012-10-10T11:29:57.370Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "egyptian01"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love this recipe! I only gave it a 4 star though because I don't follow it exactly. I used another review to make some adjustments and it's amazing. No mustard, strain and deseed the cucumber. We like dill so we add 1tsp. Def. let set for at least 4hr, but overnight is the best, so flavorful!",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-14T09:25:23.453Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tracey Ferrari Posner"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We enjoyed this dip very much. \nI used full fat plain Greek yogurt because it's what I had in the fridge. I actually had a little sour cream but not enough for the whole recipe so I just went with the yogurt. I used 2 fresh garlic cloves that I grated into the mix and I omitted the mustard because it doesn't belong in Greek gyro sauce IMHO. I used fresh dill, and grated the cucumber. \n It was very close to the dip/ sauce they serve at the Greek place close to our house.\nThis is nice to have to put on gyros, Greek salad, which is what I used it for, or crudite. \nYou can feel good about eating this and it tastes really fresh!",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-05T07:28:42.217Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sara"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I tweaked this recipe a little by, after grating the cucumber, squeezing the water from them because what wasn't used was really watery the next day, and I also only used fresh garlic, no garlic powder, and added a dash of salt to taste. But it was really good. Thank you for sharing this recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2013-08-19T07:14:11.417Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SarahRCN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A++ I used one cup plain Greek yogurt, 16 oz of lowfat sour cream (I accidently bought low fat), 2 single cloves of fresh garlic pressed, one regular cucumber (de-seeded) half grated and half diced up tiny - we like the added texture and a couple dashes of garlic-salt... so it was sort of a double batch... LOVED this. I could and will make this 1000 times and eat it on everything. Thank you for your recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-09T02:15:24.330Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ben E"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used 1/4 tsp dried dill instead of fresh. Delightful! Oh, and I processed the cucumber in the blender instead of shredding.",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-08T16:12:44.730Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Auntylene"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I wasn't sure about the sauce with sour cream but it was very good. I followed the hints of others and cut out the seeds of the cucumbers and after I grated them I squeezed them out with a paper towel. It made a difference in my sauce. One of my complaints about homemade tzatziki is the way it gets watery. With this technique it didn't get watery at all and I made it over an hour before we ate. Thanks for this recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2012-11-05T17:18:11.520Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Fisherking"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good! Our sour cream had just started to mold and had to be thrown out. I substituted onion dip and cool ranch about 50/50 of each. I also was able to use fresh dill from the garden. We all liked it so much the other day I had to come back here and join the club.",
